    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Following the verified equipment failure of a key power generation unit, the Visayas grid faced a significant capacity shortfall, triggering a grid management action by authorities. The system overseer implemented a grid stability procedure, ordering an emergency load management action to prevent overloading of critical infrastructure. This data-driven escalation protocol was a direct response to a documented supply-demand imbalance, where verified weather-driven load stress met pre-existing generation shortfalls, ultimately resulting in a quantified power deficit across the region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "result-0",
        "center_kind": "result",
