        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 0
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A verified equipment failure, specifically the unexpected shutdown of a power generation unit, served as the primary catalyst for the grid crisis. This documented outage was compounded by pre-existing generation shortfalls from other long-running plant outages. The sequence illustrates how a single point of failure, when set against a backdrop of strained infrastructure, can precipitate a widespread grid incident. The analysis of this grid incident must trace the fault line from the specific tripped unit to the systemic vulnerabilities it exposed.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "how-0"
        ],
        "center": "why-0",
        "center_kind": "why",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The grid stability monitors faced a complex crisis rooted in multiple failures. The system overseer had to account for the unit's unexpected shutdown, which occurred alongside a pattern of infrastructure neglect from other long-running plant outages. These pre-existing generation shortfalls created a fragile baseline. When verified weather-driven load stress pushed demand into a thin operating margin, the energy sector entity was forced to initiate a calculated grid protection measure to maintain the island group's grid integrity.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
